{"name":"Aqua","hex":"#0ff0fe","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)","wikidata":"Q372733"},{"title":"Aqua (Chicago)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is an 82-story mixed-use skyscraper in Lakeshore East, downtown Chicago, Illinois. Designed by a team led by Jeanne Gang of Studio Gang Architects, with James Loewenberg of Loewenberg & Associates as the Architect of Record, it includes five levels of parking below ground. The building's eighty-story, 140,000 sq ft (13,000 m2) base is topped by a 82,550 sq ft (7,669 m2) terrace with gardens, gazebos, pools, hot tubs, a walking/running track and a fire pit. Each floor covers approximately 16,000 sq ft (1,500 m2)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Aqua_%28Chicago%29_logo.png/330px-Aqua_%28Chicago%29_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(Chicago)","wikidata":"Q622895"},{"title":"Aqua (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua was a Danish eurodance band, best known for their 1997 single \"Barbie Girl\". The group formed in 1995 in Copenhagen and achieved international success around the world in the late 1990s and early 2000s. The band released three albums: Aquarium in 1997, Aquarius in 2000 and Megalomania in 2011. The group sold an estimated 33 million albums and singles, making them the most profitable Danish band ever."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_30.jpg/330px-Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_30.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(band)","wikidata":"Q213388"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/500px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/1280px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg/500px-Aqua_%28Building%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAqua_(Building)_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg/250px-AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg/500px-AquaTower2009_02_08_image2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_